    "narrative": "The Austin Waves open today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our anchor, commanding a 68.57 efficiency score. Despite facing Max Meyer, **Henderson** benefits from a strong platoon advantage (+14%) and the premium production expected from the leadoff spot (+10%), making him our most reliable engine for R and HR production. **Brady House** also presents a compelling case at 63.19; he draws a favorable matchup against Woods Richardson, where a combination of a hitter-friendly park and a robust SP skill rating (+19%) provides him a higher ceiling than his mid-order peers. **Jackson Merrill** maintains a solid 60.00, buoyed by a strong SP skill matchup against the vulnerable Matthew Liberatore, even with the inherent risk of his pending lineup slot.\n\nThe optimizer\u2019s toughest call today centered on the benching of **Josh Jung**, whose 53.97 score narrowly missed our active threshold. While **Jung** offers respectable upside against Paul Blackburn, the marginal nature of his projection made him the odd man out in favor of the higher-ceiling versatility of **Nasim Nunez** and **Marcell Ozuna**. **Nunez** remains a priority start for our squad specifically due to the scarcity of stolen bases; despite the penalty for hitting ninth, his speed profile is essential for our 5x5 objectives. Conversely, **Liam Hicks** carries the most volatility today; his 41.38 score is heavily penalized by a tough platoon dynamic against the lefty Cade Povich, and we are monitoring his lineup status closely to ensure he remains in the #2 spot as projected. \n\nWe are tracking several \"Lineup Pending\" designations across the board for **Liam Hicks**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Marcell Ozuna**, which introduces a degree of situational risk to these projections. With **Kyle Tucker** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** off the schedule today, our depth will be tested, but we remain positioned to capitalize on the weak SP_xERA marks for Woods Richardson and Liberatore. While **Coby Mayo** remains on the bench due to his low projected floor and late-order placement, he remains on standby should the weather or late-breaking lineup changes force a pivot for **Brady House** or **Nasim Nunez**.",
